I don't buy it.  Setting aside "ascension" for the moment, does playing
the racket actually diminish the chances of getting to the quest?  I
don't think it does.  

If you are the sort of player who actually entertains prospects of
ascending any and every starting character, with a specific percentage
goal in mind, you're already so experienced that one person's early game  
strategy or another's ought to make little difference.   You know how to
manage the game clock, you know how to work the movement rules, and you
know how to anticipate all kinds of stuff.  

A character who is still level 1 or 2, who has not descended below, say,
level 7, but who has a substantially negative armor class, a large dog
or two (or possibly even a real pet already), mithril armor, gloves,
and a decent collection of items that are at least BUC'd, has a
fantastically better shot at ascension than that same character at turn
one.  


